cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Bank Regulatory Data Dictionary"
message: "If you use this dataset, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Anderson
    given-names: Nicholas
    email: nickawebbox@gmail.com
    affiliation: "The New School for Social Research"
    # orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000"  # Nick to fill
repository-code: "https://github.com/andenick/bank-data-dictionary"
abstract: >-
  A detailed open catalogue of U.S. bank regulatory data: every major information
  collection and its subschedules, the MDRM code system, the FFIEC NIC
  institutional-structure data, the identifier crosswalk, cross-form mappings, and
  reconciliation formulas. v10.0 documents all 22 FR Y-9C schedules plus Call
  Report line items across 42 collections, ships a Relationship Registry of 7,539
  relationships, and enforces 100% MDRM/UBPR token validity (11,126/11,126,
  CI-enforced), empirically validated against 208 million FR Y-9C rows and 1.9
  billion Call Report rows.
keywords:
  - banking
  - regulatory-data
  - mdrm
  - ffiec
  - call-report
  - fr-y-9c
version: "10.0"
date-released: "2026-06-11"
